{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-275301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a\\times c=2i-j$ and $b\\times c=-4i+3j.$ Find $(6a-5b)\\times (2c).$\n\n$(6a-5b)\\times (2c)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$j$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-275301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the following properties of the cross product:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use the distributive property:\n\n$$\n(6a-5b)\\times (2c)=(6a)\\times (2c)-(5b)\\times (2c)\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6a)\\times (2c)-(5b)\\times (2c) & =(6\\cdot 2)(a\\times c)-(5\\cdot 2)(b\\times c) \\\\  & =12(a\\times c)-10(b\\times c)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we substitute the given values for $a\\times c$ and $b\\times c,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(a\\times c)-10(b\\times c) & =12(2i-j)-10(-4i+3j) \\\\  & =24i-12j+40i-30j \\\\  & =64\\,i-42\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-275301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "72fe37eb09cf04a3c9a08d4f90f6f21a352249f1486561e9b4009ffa9c5884a0"} {"question" "q-275301" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-275301" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "64"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-275301" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-275301" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "42"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-19767" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(3a-5b)\\times (2c)$, if $a\\times c=6i-2j$ and $b\\times c=-3i-2j.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-19767" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the following properties of the cross product:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use distributive property:\n\n$$\n(3a-5b)\\times (2c)=(3a)\\times (2c)-(5b)\\times (2c)\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3a)\\times (2c)-(5b)\\times (2c) & =(3\\cdot 2)(a\\times c)-(5\\cdot 2)(b\\times c) \\\\  & =6(a\\times c)-10(b\\times c)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we substitute the given values for $a\\times c$ and $b\\times c,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(a\\times c)-10(b\\times c) & =6(6i-2j)-10(-3i-2j) \\\\  & =36i-12j+30i+20j \\\\  & =66i+8j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-19767" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "72fe37eb09cf04a3c9a08d4f90f6f21a352249f1486561e9b4009ffa9c5884a0"} {"question" "q-19767" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-19767" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-66i-8j"] ["math" "-6i+32j"] ["math" "36i-8j"] ["math" "66i+32j"] ["math" "66i+8j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-19767" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "66i+8j"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-280351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $c\\times a=3i-2j$ and $c\\times b=4i+j.$ Find $c\\times (a+2b).$\n\n$c\\times (a+2b)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$i$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-280351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the following properties of the cross product:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use the distributive property:\n\n$$\nc\\times (a+2b)=c\\times a+c\\times (2b)\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\nc\\times a+c\\times (2b)=c\\times a+2(c\\times b)\n$$\n\n- Finally, we substitute the given values for $c\\times a$ and $c\\times b,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\times a+2(c\\times b) & =(3i-2j)+2(4i+j) \\\\  & =3i-2j+8i+2j \\\\  & =11\\,i\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-280351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "72fe37eb09cf04a3c9a08d4f90f6f21a352249f1486561e9b4009ffa9c5884a0"} {"question" "q-280351" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-280351" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-19764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(a+4b)\\times c$, if $a\\times c=8i+2j$ and $b\\times c=-2i+j.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-19764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the following properties of the cross product:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use distributive property:\n\n$$\n(a+4b)\\times c=a\\times c+(4b)\\times c\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n  \n\n$$\na\\times c+(4b)\\times c=a\\times c+4(b\\times c)\n$$\n\n- Finally, we substitute the given values for $a\\times c$ and $b\\times c,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times c+4(b\\times c) & =(8i+2j)+4(-2i+j) \\\\  & =8i+2j-8i+4j \\\\  & =6j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-19764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "72fe37eb09cf04a3c9a08d4f90f6f21a352249f1486561e9b4009ffa9c5884a0"} {"question" "q-19764" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-19764" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-6j"] ["math" "-8i+6j"] ["math" "16i+6j"] ["math" "6j"] ["math" "8i"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-19764" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6j"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-275297" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a\\times c=3i+j$ and $b\\times c=2i+2j.$ Find $(4a-3b)\\times c.$\n\n$(4a-3b)\\times c=$\n{{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$j$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-275297" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the following properties of the cross product:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use the distributive property:\n\n$$\n(4a-3b)\\times c=(4a)\\times c-(3b)\\times c\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\n(4a)\\times c-(3b)\\times c=4(a\\times c)-3(b\\times c)\n$$\n\n- Finally, we substitute the given values for $a\\times c$ and $b\\times c,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(a\\times c)-3(b\\times c) & =4(3i+j)-3(2i+2j) \\\\  & =12i+4j-6i-6j \\\\  & =6\\,i-2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-275297" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "72fe37eb09cf04a3c9a08d4f90f6f21a352249f1486561e9b4009ffa9c5884a0"} {"question" "q-275297" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-275297" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-275297" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-275297" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-127858" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(7a-2b)\\times b$, if $b\\times a=⟨2,-1,6⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-127858" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we recall the following properties of the cross product:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product of parallel vectors equals the zero vector. In particular,\n\n$$\na\\times a=0.\n$$\n\n- The cross product is anticommutative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =-b\\times a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use the distributive property:\n\n$$\n(7a-2b)\\times b=(7a)\\times b-(2b)\\times b\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\n(7a)\\times b-(2b)\\times b=7(a\\times b)-2(b\\times b)\n$$\n\n- Then, we use anticommutativity, and the fact that $b\\times b=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(a\\times b)-2(b\\times b) & =7(-b\\times a)-2(0) \\\\  & =-7(b\\times a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Substitute the given value for $b\\times a$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7(b\\times a) & =-7⟨2,-1,6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-14,7,-42⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-127858" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "72fe37eb09cf04a3c9a08d4f90f6f21a352249f1486561e9b4009ffa9c5884a0"} {"question" "q-127858" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"ques