te our expression:\n\n- First, we use the distributive property:\n\n$$\na\\times (b-3a)=a\\times b-a\\times (3a)\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\na\\times b-a\\times (3a)=a\\times b-3(a\\times a)\n$$\n\n- Then, we use the anticommutativity property and the fact that $a\\times a=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b-3(a\\times a) & =-b\\times a-3(0) \\\\  & =-b\\times a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Substitute the given value for $b\\times a$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-b\\times a & =-(2i-j+4k) \\\\  & =-2i+1j+-4k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-280385" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "72fe37eb09cf04a3c9a08d4f90f6f21a352249f1486561e9b4009ffa9c5884a0"} {"question" "q-280385" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-280385" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-280385" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2e