$\n\n- The cross product of parallel vectors equals the zero vector. In particular,\n\n$$\na\\times a=0.\n$$\n\n- The cross product is anticommutative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =-b\\times a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use the distributive property:\n\n$$\n6b\\times (2a-b)=(6b)\\times (2a)-(6b)\\times b\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6b)\\times (2a)-(6b)\\times b & =(6\\cdot 2)(b\\times a)-6(b\\times b) \\\\  & =12(b\\times a)-6(b\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we use anticommutativity, and the fact that $b\\times b=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(b\\times a)-6(b\\times b) & =12(-a\\times b)-6(0) \\\\  & =-12(a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Substitute the given value for $a\\times b$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12(a\\times b) & =-12⟨2,-5,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-24,60,12⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-280834" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "72fe37eb09cf04a3c9a08d4f90f6f21a352249f1486561e9b4009ffa9c5884a0"} {"question" "q-280834" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-280834" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-24"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/140394