times (3a-2b)=a\\times (3a)-a\\times (2b)\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\na\\times (3a)-a\\times (2b)=3(a\\times a)-2(a\\times b)\n$$\n\n- Then, we use the anticommutativity property and the fact that $a\\times a=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(a\\times a)-2(a\\times b) & =3(0)-2(-b\\times a) \\\\  & =2(b\\times a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Substitute the given value for $b\\times a$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(b\\times a) & =2⟨6,0,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12,0,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-280381" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "72fe37eb09cf04a3c9a08d4f90f6f21a352249f1486561e9b4009ffa9c5884a0"} {"question" "q-280381" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-280381" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"question" "q-280381" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039468/state.json" "file_sha256" "344d87e8b28b7f2ee0cbeb5126bb43b61d59602312a185bf22c993c0df0b9fe2"} {"quest